meta {
  name: Commerce APIs
}

auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: client_credentials
  access_token_url: https://idag2.jpmorganchase.com/adfs/oauth2/token
  refresh_token_url: https://idag2.jpmorganchase.com/adfs/oauth2/token
  client_id: {{clientId}}
  client_secret: 
  scope: 
  credentials_placement: body
  credentials_id: access_token
  token_source: access_token
  token_placement: header
  token_header_prefix: Bearer
  auto_fetch_token: true
  auto_refresh_token: true
}

auth:oauth2:additional_params:access_token_req:body {
  resource: {{resourceId}}
  client_assertion_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer
  client_assertion: {{JWSPayload}}
}

auth:oauth2:additional_params:refresh_token_req:body {
  resource: {{resourceId}}
  client_assertion_type: urn:ietf:params:oauth:client-assertion-type:jwt-bearer
  client_assertion: {{JWSPayload}}
}

script:pre-request {
  bru.setVar('cvv', String(Math.floor(100 + Math.random() * 900)));
  bru.setVar('cvv4', String(Math.floor(1000 + Math.random() * 9000)));
  const areaCode = Math.floor(200 + Math.random() * 800);   // NANP area code, first digit 2-9
  const line = 100 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 100);        // 100-199
  bru.setVar('phoneNumber', `${areaCode}5550${line}`);       // nnn + 555 + 0 + mmm
  
}

tests {
  const status = res.status ?? res.statusCode;
  
  if (typeof status !== "number" || status < 200 || status >= 300) {
    throw new Error(`Expected a 2xx response, received ${status}`);
  }
}

docs {
  # J.P. Morgan Payments — Merchant Services
  
  ## Usage
  
  1. Fill in the user-supplied secret variables in Bruno's secrets tab: `clientId`, `kid`, `merchantId`, `gOauth_Priv_Key`, and `resourceId`. The token request scripts populate `JWSPayload` and `auth-token` automatically.
  2. Run **JWT and Access Token.bru** (or **Only Access Token.bru** if you already have a signed client assertion) to exchange credentials for an access token. Collection-level OAuth2 (client credentials) is already configured in `collection.bru` to auto-fetch and auto-refresh tokens for every subsequent request.
  3. Open any folder (e.g. `Checkout/`, `Online Payments/`, `3-D Secure/`) and send a request. Pre-request and post-response scripts populate the environment variables (`transactionId`, `consumerprofileid`, etc.) that dependent requests rely on.
  
  > For step-by-step integration guides and full field documentation, see the official [J.P. Morgan Payments documentation](https://developer.payments.jpmorgan.com/docs/home) on the Payments Developer Portal.
  
  ## Runbooks
  
  Both `Checkout/` and `Online Payments/` contain a `00 Runbook` folder — an ordered, step-by-step walkthrough of that product's capabilities. Each numbered step folder has its own `docs` note (visible on the folder in Bruno) with a link to the matching guide on the official Payments Developer Portal. Open the folder for the area you're working on and follow the link there for the full request/response field reference.
  
  ## Entitlements
  
  Some actions are entitlement-gated per merchant ID, per brand or function (e.g. Account Updater by brand — Discover, Mastercard, Visa; 3-D Secure as a function). Requests for actions your `merchantId` isn't entitled to will fail; that is expected.
}
